Compound tenses such as [[Perfect (grammar)|perfect]] and [[pluperfect]] are formed with the verb {{Lang|sia|ĺii̭je}} in the present or imperfect as [[Auxiliary verb|auxiliary]], and the [[participle]] of the main verb. Examples are {{Lang|sia|ĺam tĭĕhtmi̮nč}} ‘I have known’ from {{Lang|sia|tĭĕhttɛ}} ‘to know’, and {{Lang|sia|ĺai tui̭jāma}} ‘(s)he had made’ from {{Lang|sia|tui̭je}} ‘to make’.

The conditional mood has the marker ''-č'', which is added to the weak grade of the stem: {{Lang|sia|kuarčim}} ‘I would sew’, {{Lang|sia|vizzčik}} ‘you (sg.) would become tired’.

